### Security Audit
**Risk:** Floating point precision drift risk when unwinding queued decay. Accumulating `undoneCredit = reduce((total, e) => total + e.amount, 0)` and subtracting it in one step causes IEEE 754 float precision loss differences compared to the individual `COMMONS_BALANCE += decayedAmount` operations performed during decay application. Across repeated `loadState()` calls on high-volume accounts, this micro-drift can slowly mint or burn fractional bean dust.

**Suggested Fix:**
Subtract each queued decay amount individually (or in reverse order of addition) to maintain exact float operation parity:
```typescript
for (let i = this.decayEvents.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
    COMMONS_BALANCE -= this.decayEvents[i].amount;
}
```
